r could affect calmness under pressure. Candidate B's nasty remarks also affect crew. Candidate C's communication difficulty is also serious. Candidate A's show-off may be less severe than hot temper? Not open to new ideas may affect adaptability.\n\nWe need to pick one. I think Candidate D seems balanced: good reliability, stress, technical, responsibility, concentration. The hot temper is a concern but maybe manageable. Candidate B's weak memory for numbers is a safety-critical issue. Candidate C's communication difficulty is also safety-critical. Candidate A's not open to new ideas may affect adaptability.\n\nThus I will recommend Candidate D, but note concerns.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion: none, but we can say \"Given the facts we have so far\". That's okay.\n\nProvide evidence: D concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously (strengths). Concern: hot temper, know-it-all (cooperation). Explain why still best.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate D\"."}
